      "senses": [
        {
          "definition": "The adverb points to a place identified in context, as when Yahweh plants a garden and places the man there. With מִן it means ‘from there’.",
          "evidence": [
            {
              "ref": "Gen.2.8",
              "role": "defining"
            },
            {
              "note": "The river waters the garden, and וּמִשָּׁם ‘and from there’ points back to the garden as the place from which it divides.",
              "ref": "Gen.2.10",
              "role": "example"
            },
            {
              "ref": "Gen.12.8"
            },
            {
              "note": "In אֲשֶׁר לֻקַּח מִשָּׁם, שָׁם points back to the ground and מִן identifies it as the place from which the man was taken.",
              "ref": "Gen.3.23",
              "role": "defining"
            }
          ],
          "gloss": "there, to that place"
        }
      ]
    },
